  "description": "Per-eigenvalue, signed-character, operator-trace promotion of the scalar Φ_q brane-tower probe. For each isotope in {D, T, ³He} and each k in {1,2,3,4,5,6,8,10}, computes tower_op^(k) = |Σ_λ y_λ(q_0) · tr_λ(Φ_q^{[≤k]}(ρ_λ(β)))| where ρ_λ(β) is the numerical braid operator in irrep V_λ (via Hoefsmit seminormal at q_0). Eigenvalues μ_a^(λ) via numpy.linalg.eigvals; Φ_q applied per eigenvalue; operator-trace = Σ_a Φ_q^{[≤k]}(μ_a^(λ)); Wedderburn-summed with signed y_λ (complex), final |·| at binding-formula level. Replaces the prior _avg_chi_over_classical_dim variant which used three approximations (classical dim, abs χ, mean-of-eigenvalues) that biased the result.",
